(5 Where to put the unit) Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Clearances for air flow and service: front \(air outlet\) 1500 mm, rear \(air inlet\) 600 mm, service) Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
(side 800 mm, other side 300 mm, above 2000 mm. The clearances are the same for all four models. Do) Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
(not blow the outlet air towards a neighbour's windows or a footpath where ice could form.) Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Put the unit on a level concrete base at least 150 mm above ground, with the anti-vibration feet) Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
(supplied. The base carries at least 1.5 times the unit's weight. Lead the condensate to a frost-free) Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
(drain; in frost the unit makes up to 12 litres of condensate an hour \(HX-80: 30 litres\).) Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj T*
/F2 10 Tf
(6 Water side) Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Flush the system before connecting the unit. Fit the strainer supplied in the return, with shut-off) Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
(valves on both sides. Fit flexible connections of at least 500 mm. Fill with water of pH 8.2 to 10.0) Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
(and a hardness of at most 8.4 degrees dH; harder water must be softened. Pressure test the circuit) Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
(at 4.5 bar for 2 hours; set the cold system pressure to 1.5 bar.) Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
(The buffer tank must hold at least the volume in section 2 so that defrosting has enough energy.) Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Without it the unit shows fault F212 in frost.) Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj T*
/F2 10 Tf
(7 Electrical) Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
(400 V three-phase with neutral, through its own circuit with the fuse in section 2 and a residual) Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
(current device of type B, 300 mA. The controller needs a separate 230 V supply, fused at 10 A.) Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Sensor cables are laid at least 200 mm away from power cables. The utility's blocking signal is) Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
(wired to terminals 21 and 22.) Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj T*
/F2 10 Tf
(8 Cascade) Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Up to 8 units can run as a cascade under one lead controller. Units of different sizes can be mixed;) Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
(the lead unit is the one with the lowest bus address. Each unit needs its own strainer and its own) Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
(non-return valve.) Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj T*
/F2 10 Tf
(9 Handover) Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Commissioning is done by a Veltra-certified technician and reported to Veltra within 14 days; the) Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
(warranty starts on the commissioning date only when the report arrived in time, otherwise on the) Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
(delivery date.) Tj T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj T*
